{"about_the_game":"<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Gameplay</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A<strong> 32</strong>\u00a0player story that unfolds over\u00a0<strong>3 </strong>real-world days</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A unique\u00a0<strong>&quot;2nd-person&quot;</strong>\u00a0combat system, featuring a combination of\u00a0<strong>shooter</strong> and <strong>melee</strong> gameplay</p></li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Story</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>300 Years Ago</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The Tower was discovered during maritime exploration. Early human expeditions vanished without a trace, cementing its reputation as a place of mystery, danger, and legend.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>50 Years Ago</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >With advances in AI, autonomous robots were deployed into the Tower to explore its depths. However, all attempts failed. Traditional wireless communication was disrupted inside the Tower, and no meaningful data was ever recovered, leaving its interior a complete unknown.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Present Day</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Advancements in neutrino communication enabled the development of the Akasha System, allowing humans to remotely pilot SSFrames\u2014mechanized bodies\u2014into the Tower, accompanied by automata for support. These expeditions have uncovered extraordinary resources: plants that extend human lifespan, and vast, untapped energy sources. In response, the Tower Delver Association was founded to manage exploration and extract these valuable discoveries.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >&quot;Welcome Recruit&quot;</p>","background":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/2560720?t=1771463278","background_raw":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/2560720?t=1771463278","capsule_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/ste